From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hjviewer <haejin.cho@yonsei.ac.kr>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 21:59:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 076/161] hjviewer: tokens that pass contrast, Korean line
 breaks

U23: the peer cards, rows and the ID field's suggestions draw the
online state with hjvOnlineDot (hjv_style.dart): a filled dot in the
palette's success colour when online, a hollow ring in textTertiary
when offline, in place of Material's green and the orange kColorWarn,
which told them apart by colour alone. Each card gives a screen reader
one label (name, online state, platform, user@host, note) in place of
its pieces and their tooltips; the menu button keeps its own node.

U46: the palette keeps its hierarchy with new values: textTertiary
New tokens dangerText (#C8321F light, #F97066 dark) for danger as
text, and primaryFill/primaryFillHover (#1E6FD9/#1659BE light,
theme's elevated buttons, the FAB, the CM's buttons, the phone's
connect button and locked keycaps. Hover and press darken a fill
instead of lightening it. Text on primarySoft or fill (the settings
side bar, the ID's name, the side list, the note block's and the
update callout's buttons) is primaryStrong. colorScheme.error is
dangerText, error lines are 13 px, the menus' delete, remove and log
out texts use dangerText. Check boxes get a textTertiary border and
switches a textSecondary thumb when off in both themes, the password
fields' eye icon is textSecondary, and under high contrast (iOS
Increase Contrast, Windows high contrast) fields get a thin border.

U47: hjvKeepAll (hjv_style.dart) puts U+2060 WORD JOINER between the
characters of each word with Hangul, so Korean lines break only at
spaces (CSS word-break: keep-all); other words stay as they are. It
is applied on the widget side only (not in _t, so tests and the texts
sent to Rust are unchanged): A1, A2 and P2's bodies and hint, the
P1/P2/G2 card, G1, G3 and the other note blocks' texts.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
